  "description": "Write CUDA C/C++ kernels inline inside C# source files using raw string literals, annotate\n      a partial method with [GpuKernel], and let the Roslyn source generator invoke nvcc at build\n      time. The resulting multi-arch fatbinary is embedded directly in your assembly — no separate\n      .ptx files, no CUDA Runtime API, no manual P/Invoke.  Supports strongly-typed CudaBuffer<T>\n      device pointers, parallel multi-kernel compilation, gzip-compressed fatbin embedding, and\n      zero-configuration GPU detection at runtime via the CUDA Driver API.",
  "id": "KernelSharp",
